{"i": 25, "key": "ig2b02:p5:light-infantry:text-b", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 354166, 928922, 369950], "label": "Light Infantry (below counter)", "components": ["Continued prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "made them different from skirmishers."}
{"i": 26, "key": "ig2b02:p5:skirmishers", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 375631, 928922, 528410], "label": "Skirmishers inline heading and paragraph", "components": ["Skirmishers inline heading and paragraph"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Skirmishers: A generic term applied to troops that wore no ar-\nmor, rarely carried shields, and used missiles: javelinists, archers\nand slingers. Their role was to harass and annoy the approaching\nenemy and present a screen behind which, hopefully, movement\ncould be concealed. Their mobility allowed them to outrun their\nweightier opponents, which, all things considered, was their best\nbet for survival. They rarely, if ever, shock-attacked, as they had\nno weapons with which to do so, and they deployed in dispersed,\namorphous formations which gave them great flexibility in terms\nof maneuvering."}
{"i": 27, "key": "ig2b02:p5:javelinists:text-a", "kind": "clause", "box": [587418, 534090, 928922, 594697], "label": "Javelinists (beside counter)", "components": ["Javelinists inline bold heading", "Opening prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Javelinists: Skirmishers that used a thrown spear as\ntheir weapon of harassment. Essentially, the era sees\nfew pure javelinist skirmishers, as the weapon was\nproving to be inefficient when used alone, which is"}
{"i": 28, "key": "ig2b02:p5:javelinists:counter", "kind": "diagram", "box": [513071, 537878, 575981, 586490], "label": "Javelinists sample counter", "components": ["Thrace", "1", "J missile glyph", "5", "LI", "5", "5", "Soldier illustration"], "uncertainty": ["Small counter glyphs are literal observations; exact transcription and semantic interpretation remain pending."], "text": ""}
{"i": 29, "key": "ig2b02:p5:javelinists:text-b", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 595328, 928922, 641415], "label": "Javelinists (below counter)", "components": ["Continued prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "why there are no javelinist skirmishers in the game. By this time,\nmost foot soldiers carried a javelin or two which they threw\nprior to closing for combat."}
{"i": 30, "key": "ig2b02:p5:archers:text-a", "kind": "clause", "box": [587418, 646464, 928922, 707071], "label": "Archers (beside counter)", "components": ["Archers inline bold heading", "Opening prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Archers: Light troops (virtually no armor/protection),\nusually from Crete, that fired about 30+ arrows an\neffective distance of 150+ yards, with a maximum\nrange of 250 yards (less when mounted and moving)."}
{"i": 31, "key": "ig2b02:p5:archers:counter", "kind": "diagram", "box": [513071, 650883, 575981, 699495], "label": "Archers sample counter", "components": ["Crete", "2", "A missile glyph", "1", "SK", "4", "6", "Archer illustration"], "uncertainty": ["Small counter glyphs are literal observations; exact transcription and semantic interpretation remain pending."], "text": ""}
{"i": 32, "key": "ig2b02:p5:archers:text-b", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 707702, 928922, 753788], "label": "Archers (below counter)", "components": ["Continued prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "The arrows of the day could rarely pierce metal armor but were\neffective elsewhere. Cheap to arm; expensive to train. Used as\nskirmishers."}
{"i": 33, "key": "ig2b02:p5:slingers:text-a", "kind": "clause", "box": [587418, 759469, 928922, 820076], "label": "Slingers (beside counter)", "components": ["Slingers inline bold heading", "Opening prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Slingers: Another unarmored skirmisher type. They\nhurled pellets, usually made of lead, an effective dis-\ntance of up to 120+ yards, although accuracy was\nnowhere near that of arrows. Cheap to arm but requir-"}
{"i": 34, "key": "ig2b02:p5:slingers:counter", "kind": "diagram", "box": [513071, 763257, 575981, 811869], "label": "Slingers sample counter", "components": ["Bal'ric", "6", "S missile glyph", "1", "SK", "3", "6", "Slinger illustration"], "uncertainty": ["Small counter glyphs are literal observations; exact transcription and semantic interpretation remain pending."], "text": ""}
{"i": 35, "key": "ig2b02:p5:slingers:text-b", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 820707, 928922, 866793], "label": "Slingers (below counter)", "components": ["Continued prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "ing a fair amount of skilled training, slingers took up a lot of space.\nThe wind-up radius was 2-3x greater than that of other skirmish-\ner units. The Balearic Islands produced most of these troops."}
{"i": 36, "key": "ig2b02:p5:light-cavalry:text-a", "kind": "clause", "box": [587418, 872474, 928922, 933713], "label": "Light Cavalry (beside counter)", "components": ["Light Cavalry inline bold heading", "Opening prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Light Cavalry: Essentially, mounted javelinists\nnoted for their mobility. That speed and mobility\ncould be a major plus was demonstrated by the ef-\nfectiveness of Masanissa�s and Maharbal�s magnifi-"}
{"i": 37, "key": "ig2b02:p5:light-cavalry:counter", "kind": "diagram", "box": [513071, 876262, 575981, 924874], "label": "Light Cavalry sample counter", "components": ["Nmdia", "1", "J missile glyph", "4", "LC", "8", "9", "Mounted soldier illustration"], "uncertainty": ["Small counter glyphs are literal observations; exact transcription and semantic interpretation remain pending."], "text": ""}
