{"i": 117, "key": "ig2b02:p8:path-enemy-zoc", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 200757, 487746, 217172], "label": "4.21 bullet: enemy ZOC", "components": ["4.21 bullet: enemy ZOC"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "\u2022 a hex in an enemy Zone of Control (ZOC)"}
{"i": 118, "key": "ig2b02:p8:path-terrain", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 217803, 487746, 234218], "label": "4.21 bullet: impassable terrain", "components": ["4.21 bullet: impassable terrain"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "\u2022 or terrain a leader could not cross or enter."}
{"i": 119, "key": "ig2b02:p8:range-calculation", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 239267, 487746, 286617], "label": "4.21 Friendly unit negation and instant range calculation", "components": ["4.21 Friendly unit negation and instant range calculation"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Friendly units negate enemy ZOCs for purposes of tracing order\npaths. All other paths are considered unobstructed. Command\nRanges are calculated at the instant the order is given."}
{"i": 120, "key": "ig2b02:p8:individual-effects", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 291666, 487746, 369319], "label": "4.22 IO actions/count/Finished side", "components": ["4.22 IO actions/count/Finished side"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.22 An IO allows one friendly unit to conduct movement and/\nor Missile Fire, be rallied, etc., per 5.22. In each Orders Phase, a\nleader may issue a number of IOs equal to his Initiative Rating.\nOnce a leader can give no more orders and cannot be activated\nagain, flip the leader counter to its Finished side."}
{"i": 121, "key": "ig2b02:p8:leader-movement", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 374368, 487746, 451389], "label": "4.23 Leader movement", "components": ["4.23 Leader movement"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.23 A leader may give an IO to move himself, which counts\nagainst the number of orders that leader may issue in that Orders\nPhase. A leader may instead issue an Individual Order to a unit\nwith which he is stacked and move along with it. The leader must\nremain with the moving combat unit and end up in the same hex."}
{"i": 122, "key": "ig2b02:p8:enemy-zoc-orders", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 457070, 487746, 549243], "label": "4.24 Enemy ZOC and OC", "components": ["4.24 Enemy ZOC and OC"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.24 A leader, other than the Overall Commander (OC), who is\nin an enemy ZOC may not issue orders either to combat units\nor to himself, and thus may not move out of that enemy ZOC\nunless and until he is moved out of that ZOC by an IO from the\nOC (4.4). While in an enemy ZOC, the only IO an OC may issue\nis to move himself. See also 5.26."}
{"i": 123, "key": "ig2b02:p8:finished-leader", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 554292, 487746, 586490], "label": "4.25 Finished leader", "components": ["4.25 Finished leader"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.25 A leader who is Finished (5.15) may not issue orders.\nHowever, he may move, but only if ordered by his OC to do so."}
{"i": 124, "key": "ig2b02:p8:line-heading", "kind": "heading", "box": [71895, 595328, 487746, 614899], "label": "4.3 LEADER CAPABILITIES: LINE COMMANDS", "components": ["4.3 LEADER CAPABILITIES: LINE COMMANDS"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.3 LEADER CAPABILITIES: LINE COMMANDS"}
{"i": 125, "key": "ig2b02:p8:line-orders", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 615530, 487746, 768309], "label": "4.31 Line Commands", "components": ["4.31 Line Commands"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.31 An eligible leader, instead of issuing Individual Orders,\nmay issue one or more Line Commands (given by the Line Com-\nmand Rating). Each Line Command allows the leader to order\nany/all combat units that comprise a Line (4.32). The units that\nmay comprise a Line are listed on the Line Command Eligibility\nChart for each scenario. There is no limit to the number of units\nin a Line that may be so ordered, and all the eligible units in a\nLine do not have to take part. Units in a Line do not have to stay\ntogether when they move, although to do otherwise is to court\norganizational disaster."}
{"i": 126, "key": "ig2b02:p8:line-composition-left", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 773358, 487746, 926768], "label": "4.32 Line Composition left-column paragraph", "components": ["4.32 Line Composition left-column paragraph"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.32 Line Composition: In a reflection of training and discipline\nlevels, as well as tactical usage, the units in most lines must be\nadjacent. Any space between units ends the line. In certain other\nlines, each unit must be within 2 (and occasionally 3) hexes of at\nleast one other unit in the line. If there is an intervening space,\nit may not be occupied by an enemy unit, a friendly unit from\na different line (Skirmishers and Velites are an exception, see\n9.2), or an enemy ZOC. The units which may use a two-space\n(or three-space) Line are noted on the scenario\u2019s Line Command\nEligibility Chart."}
{"i": 127, "key": "ig2b02:p8:line-composition-right", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 66287, 928922, 174874], "label": "4.32 continuation at top of right column", "components": ["4.32 continuation at top of right column"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "A Line can be of any length provided that the units meet the ad-\njacency requirements and all the units in the Line have the same\norientation\u2014either Flank-to-Flank or (but not and) Front-to-Rear\n(see 7.1). For units In Column, treat the Flank hexes adjacent to\nthe Rear hex as Rear hexes. If the units meet the adjacency re-\nquirements, but do not have the same orientation, only those units\nwithin the leader\u2019s Command Range can be included in the Line."}
{"i": 128, "key": "ig2b02:p8:cannae-example", "kind": "example", "box": [513071, 179292, 928922, 272096], "label": "Cannae deployment EXAMPLE", "components": ["Cannae deployment EXAMPLE"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "EXAMPLE: In the initial deployment for Cannae, the Carthag-\ninian Left Wing cavalry meets the Line eligibility requirements\nbecause they are all adjacent to each other and within Has-\ndrubal\u2019s Command Range. The Roman Velites are adjacent and\nFlank-to-Flank so all can be included in the Line without being\nwithin a leader\u2019s Command Range."}
{"i": 129, "key": "ig2b02:p8:line-historical-note", "kind": "note", "box": [513071, 275252, 928922, 371844], "label": "Historical note on scenario line adjustments", "components": ["Historical note on scenario line adjustments"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "HISTORICAL NOTE: Individual scenario adjustments to this\nrule reflect tactical theory in different periods. For example, at\nBeneventum, the Triarii cannot use a two-space Line because\nof the tactical theory that they were a Phalanx-like last line of\ndefense. By Bagradas Plains, the Romans had seen what el-\nephants could do to such a line and adjusted wisely (if not well)."}
{"i": 130, "key": "ig2b02:p8:line-eligibility", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 382575, 928922, 535985], "label": "4.33 Line Command Eligibility", "components": ["4.33 Line Command Eligibility"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "4.33 Line Command Eligibility: A leader\u2019s ability to issue\na Line Command depends on his position in the command\nhierarchy and the type of Orders Phase. When giving a Line\nCommand, the leader must start his Orders Phase within 2 hexes\nof\u2014and have a clear LOS (8.14) to\u2014at least one unit in that\nline. Elephants do not block LOS in this case. The leader cannot\nbe in an enemy ZOC. Those OCs with a 2 LC capability (e.g.,\nHannibal) must start the Orders Phase within the 2-hex range of\nboth Lines to which they issue the LC. They may not issue one\nLC, move, and then issue another."}
{"i": 131, "key": "ig2b02:p8:overall-heading", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 543560, 928922, 560607], "label": "Overall Commanders", "components": ["Overall Commanders"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Overall Commanders"}
{"i": 132, "key": "ig2b02:p8:overall-prose", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 561237, 928922, 592804], "label": "Overall Commanders paragraph", "components": ["Overall Commanders paragraph"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "The Overall Commander (OC) may issue Line Command(s) in\nhis Initial and Momentum-generated Orders Phases."}
{"i": 133, "key": "ig2b02:p8:subordinate-heading", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 600378, 928922, 617425], "label": "Subordinate Commanders", "components": ["Subordinate Commanders"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Subordinate Commanders"}
{"i": 134, "key": "ig2b02:p8:subordinate-introduction", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 618055, 928922, 649622], "label": "Subordinate Commanders introduction", "components": ["Subordinate Commanders introduction"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "A Subordinate Commander may issue Line Command(s) in his\nInitial (non-Momentum) Orders Phase if:"}
{"i": 135, "key": "ig2b02:p8:subordinate-condition-one", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 651515, 928922, 683713], "label": "Condition 1 including printed or", "components": ["Condition 1 including printed or"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "1. he starts his Orders Phase within his OC\u2019s Command Range;\nor"}
{"i": 136, "key": "ig2b02:p8:subordinate-condition-two", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 684974, 928922, 761995], "label": "Condition 2 die roll and modifiers", "components": ["Condition 2 die roll and modifiers"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "2. he is outside his OC\u2019s Command Range, and the owning\nplayer rolls a die, applying a +1 DRM if any of the units in\nthat proposed line are in an enemy ZOC, and that die roll is\nthe same as or lower than the OC\u2019s Strategy Rating. If it is\nhigher, he may issue only Individual Orders."}
{"i": 137, "key": "ig2b02:p8:exception-one", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 767045, 928922, 799243], "label": "Exception #1", "components": ["Exception #1"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Exception #1: In the first Game Turn only, the leader may\nautomatically issue LCs regardless of his proximity to the OC."}
{"i": 138, "key": "ig2b02:p8:exception-two", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 804292, 928922, 835859], "label": "Exception #2", "components": ["Exception #2"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Exception #2: See Carthaginian Command (4.6), which super-\nsedes all the above."}
{"i": 139, "key": "ig2b02:p8:subordinate-momentum", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 841540, 928922, 903410], "label": "Momentum-generated Orders Phase paragraph", "components": ["Momentum-generated Orders Phase paragraph"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "A Subordinate Commander may issue a Line Command in a Mo-\nmentum-generated Orders Phase only if the player rolls against\nthe OC\u2019s Strategy Rating per #2 above. The leader cannot issue\na Line Command if he did not do so in his Initial Orders Phase."}
{"i": 140, "key": "ig2b02:p8:copyright-footer", "kind": "editorial", "box": [426470, 945707, 573530, 960228], "label": "Copyright footer", "components": ["Copyright symbol", "2026 GMT Games, LLC"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "\u00a9 2026 GMT Games, LLC"}

